# aros-safe-overwrite
#
# On AROS, opening an existing file with O_TRUNC - what fopen("wb") and std::ofstream do - silently loses the data: the open succeeds, the writes report the full count, close() returns 0, and the file reads back as 0 bytes, permanently. Measured 4/4 on FAT32 and confirmed after a guest restart; creating and deleting files both work. So remove the target first and let the caller create it fresh, at all four write sites: saved games (FileStream), the configuration, scores.dat and screenshots. A no-op on every other platform. This does NOT give atomicity - a write that fails halfway now loses the previous contents - which is no worse than today, where the file is destroyed even on success; the temp-file-and-rename refinement is a tracked follow-up, and rename() was measured to work here.
#
# Against OpenLoco af445f8dc6632c6341fc7b26c3246685406e6815, applied with -p1 by scripts/bootstrap.sh.
# Saved 2026-09-17.

